---
title: FAQ — Things 4 Good
description: Common questions about the Things 4 Good candle fundraiser — how it works, what it costs, where the money goes, preorders, and the 2026 sale.
card:
  kicker: "Good questions"
  name: "The details, answered."
  summary: "Everything about the candles, the sale, and where your donation goes."
  photo: faq
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<!-- ============================ HEADER ============================ -->
<section class="section page-head" id="head">
  <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">&larr; Things 4 Good</a>
    <p class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center">Good questions</p>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5.4vw,4rem);letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.02">The details, answered.</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin:18px auto 0;text-align:center">Everything about the candles, the sale, and where your donation goes. Don&rsquo;t see your question? <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:700;text-decoration:none">Email a Thing</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ FAQ ============================ -->
<section class="section" id="faq" style="padding-top:clamp(20px,3vw,40px)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="faq">
      <details class="qa reveal" open>
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="make">So you really make the candles? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Yes! It&rsquo;s not rocket science, but we like to pretend that it is. 😄 We hand-pour every one. We all pitch in on ordering supplies, mixing, pouring and setting wicks. Then we wait for them to cure and add the labels, which Mazie draws.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="money">What happens to the money you raise? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">We track every purchase during the sale, and you can split your donation however you like across the four non-profits we picked. After the weekend we add it all up and send the donations. We pay for the materials ourselves, and obviously our labor is free. <b>The full price of every candle goes to the non-profits.</b> Since 2021 that&rsquo;s added up to <a href="/stats/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">${{ metrics.grandTotalDisplay }} across {{ metrics.orgCount }} organizations</a>.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="cost">How much do candles cost? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Each candle is a <b>$25 donation</b>, the same price it&rsquo;s been every year. You can pay whatever way is easiest:
          <div class="pay"><span>Venmo</span><span>Cash App</span><span>Apple Pay</span><span>Zelle</span><span>Cash</span><span>Check</span></div>
          Venmo <b>@{{ site.payment.venmo }}</b> is the favorite. Every handle is on the <a href="/pay/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">payment page</a>.
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="donate">Can I support the fundraiser if I don&rsquo;t need candles? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Yes! Every year a few people just send a donation, add a little extra to their candle donation, or join in from too far away to pick up candles. It all counts. Send it any way on the <a href="/pay/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">payment page</a> and tell us how you&rsquo;d like it split across the four causes, or we can divide it evenly.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="choose">Can I choose which causes my money supports? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Yes, that&rsquo;s the whole idea! Each year the four of us each pick a cause we care about, and you decide how to split your donation across them. Support one, support all four, or ask for a specific split. Some folks do. (Choosing is for purchases at the sale. Preorders are divided evenly.) Want to see who picked what over the years? Browse <a href="/impact/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">the full list</a>.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="preorder">Can I preorder candles? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Yes! If you&rsquo;re ordering <b>six or more</b>, {% if site.preorderSheet %}fill out our <a href="{{ site.preorderSheet }}" data-tinylytics-event="preorder.sheet" data-tinylytics-event-value="faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">preorder form</a> and Jamie will email you a payment link.{% else %}the preorder sheet opens closer to the sale and goes to subscribers first.{% endif %} We&rsquo;ll have those candles ready to pick up anytime during the sale, and the form stays open until it ends. The details are on the <a href="/preorder/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">preorder page</a>.</div>
      </details>
      {% if site.makerNight %}
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="maker-night">What&rsquo;s Maker Night? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">An evening for six, {{ site.makerNightTime }} on {{ site.makerNightDate }}. At the fall sale we put out six gold Maker Night candles, each in a scent made only for them, for a <b>${{ site.makerNightDonation }} donation</b>. Buying one gets you a seat: on the night a thank-you candle will be waiting for you, and you&rsquo;ll hand-pour four of your own in any scents from our library. The donation is divided evenly across this year&rsquo;s four causes, 100% to good. <a href="/maker-night/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Explore Maker Night &rarr;</a></div>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="when-where">When and where is the 2026 sale? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Saturday, <b>November 7</b> and Sunday, <b>November 8, 2026</b>, in Minneapolis. Hours and the address come by email: <a href="{{ site.updatesUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="updates.click" data-tinylytics-event-value="faq-when" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">choose Candle Fundraiser updates</a>, or <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">email Jamie</a>.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="qa reveal">
        <summary data-tinylytics-event-value="growth">How has the fundraiser grown? <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="ans">Every year so far! We started at $4,757 in 2021 and reached $9,048 in 2025, our biggest year yet and up 29.1% from the year before. Thank you! The whole five-year story, candle counts and all, is on the <a href="/stats/" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Numbers page</a>. After every sale Jamie posts the results and the math on the <a href="{{ site.blogUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">blog</a> after every sale.</div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="mn-band reveal" style="margin-top:clamp(36px,5vw,56px)">
      <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="mn-copy">
        <span class="tag">Still curious?</span>
        <h3>Ask us anything.</h3>
        <p>A real Thing reads every message. We&rsquo;re always happy to talk candles, causes, or how it all works.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mn-act">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email {{ site.email }} <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a>
        <span class="small">Or <a href="{{ site.updatesUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="updates.click" data-tinylytics-event-value="faq-ask" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--marigold);font-weight:700">get Candle Fundraiser updates</a></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<script>
  // Count a question as read when it opens, not when it closes: a closed
  // question's summary carries the Tinylytics event, an open one's does not.
  // Tinylytics reads the attribute during the click, before the toggle lands.
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq details.qa').forEach((qa) => {
    const summary = qa.querySelector('summary');
    const sync = () => qa.open
      ? summary.removeAttribute('data-tinylytics-event')
      : summary.setAttribute('data-tinylytics-event', 'faq.open');
    sync();
    qa.addEventListener('toggle', sync);
  });
</script>
{% endblock %}
